Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:40:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: city programs drawn in earlier games built at start

A draw with the shared city program costs about as much as the whole city
on an Adreno, so the frames that fall back to it while a material's own
program builds take hundreds of ms. Keep the (pipeline, material) pairs
drawn once in city-programs.txt in the user folder and queue them at the
next start; pairs a frame asks for go to the front of the queue. Frames
more than 120 ms after the last one are logged with their phases and the
number of draws that used the shared program.
---
 mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs            |  17 ++++
 mcla-rs/crates/game/src/render/cityspec.rs | 108 +++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs b/mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs
index 80ef911..0c6ba92 100644
--- a/mcla-rs/crates/game/src/main.rs
